            <div xml:id="d823">

                <pb facs="1042" n="928" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg928"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">325.1121 Bethune, Larry K./2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-19T13:00:00-05:00">March 19, 1931—1
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>10. Your 21, March 18, 4 p.m. The Department reiterates the position expressed in
                    its instruction No. 604 of October 21, 1925.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d823-f1"/>
                    You should urgently renew your efforts with the appropriate authorities to be
                    permitted to communicate with Bethune and also request a like permission for his
                    counsel. What are the charges against him?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
